//? Title: Autoencoder Restoration: Noisy Pixels and Missing Patches
//? Subtitle: Three reproducible frozen models, target-free inference and exact observed-pixel copies
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Restoration applies a frozen model to a damaged observation; clean targets belong to evaluation.
This report reuses two matched dense autoencoders and one visible-only masked transformer on
200 held-out MNIST digits. Four complete native prerequisite programs reproduce the original
three-epoch checkpoints; the restoration application then makes zero additional updates.
At the training noise amplitude, denoising slightly improves on the noisy input but loses to
the matched ordinary model. For missing patches, the masked model beats zero fill and the
mismatched denoiser, but loses to a fitting-only pixel mean. All failures and unfiltered cases
remain visible. Native patch selection preserves visible pixels bit-for-bit.
)
\toc

> A damaged observation is the model input

A denoising model learns to map corrupted observations to clean targets; here it is applied
without a target, following the denoising criterion described by
[Vincent et al. (2010)](https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v11/vincent10a.html).
The masked model uses an encoder that sees visible patches only and a decoder that receives
codes, locations and mask tokens, following the asymmetric idea of
[He et al. (2021/2022)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.06377).
These small teaching networks and short fits do not reproduce either paper's benchmark setup.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/restoration_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(51, 1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle st;
  st.width     = 5.8;
  st.height    = 2.8;
  st.font_size = 18;
  d.node("n", {0, 3}, "Corrupted observation\nGaussian noise + clipping", st)
      .node("d", {8, 3}, "Frozen dense model\nObservation only", st)
      .node("o", {16, 3}, "Denoised image\nClean target used to score", st)
      .edge("n", "d")
      .edge("d", "o");
  d.node("v", {0, -4}, "Observed patches\n4 of 16 are visible", st)
      .node("e", {8, -4}, "Frozen MAE encoder\nVisible patches + locations", st)
      .node("g", {16, -4}, "Frozen MAE decoder\nCodes + locations + tokens", st)
      .node("c", {24, -4}, "Composite image\nPredicted hidden / copied visible", st)
      .edge("v", "e")
      .edge("e", "g")
      .edge("g", "c");
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke copy;
  copy.arrow = true;
  copy.color = {37, 99, 235};
  d.path({{0, -5.4}, {0, -8}, {24, -8}, {24, -5.4}}, copy)
      .text({12, -8.8}, "Visible observed pixels bypass prediction and are copied exactly", 18)
      .text(
          {12, -12},
          "Clean hidden pixels are absent from inference.\nThree frozen stores stay unchanged; the "
          "application has no optimizer.",
          20)
      .save_svg("build/restoration_method.svg");
}
