```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/restoration_masked_detail.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  const auto a    = n::load_npz("build/restoration/analysis.npz");
  auto       find = [&](const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  const auto hidden = 1. - n::sum(n::take_rows(find("selection"), {0}), {1});
  const auto mask_image =
      n::models::MaeImage(n::broadcast_to(n::expand_dims(hidden, 2), {1, 16, 49}));
  std::vector<n::Tensor> panels{
      n::take_rows(find("test_images").reshape({200, 784}), {0}),
      mask_image,
      n::take_rows(find("observed").reshape({200, 784}), {0}),
      n::take_rows(find("mae_hidden_prediction"), {0}),
      n::take_rows(find("mae_composite"), {0})};
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::concat(panels, 0).reshape({5, 28, 28, 1}),
      "build/restoration_masked_detail.png",
      5,
      0,
      1,
      4,
      220. / 255.,
      5);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/restoration_masked_detail.png)
// result_end

\caption(Columns: target, hidden mask (white=hidden), observation, raw MAE prediction and copied-visible composite. The mask, not the clean target, identifies inference locations.)
\alttext(One fixed digit is shown beside its twelve-hidden-patch mask, observed pixels, raw decoder prediction and final composite with visible pixels restored exactly.)

> A global average does not rank every individual case

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/restoration_case_errors.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  const auto a    = n::load_npz("build/restoration/analysis.npz");
  auto       find = [&](const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  const auto hidden = n::cast(1. - n::sum(find("selection"), {1}), n::DType::Float64),
             target = n::models::MaePatches(n::cast(find("test_images"), n::DType::Float64));
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> errors;
  for (const std::string name : {"mean_composite", "mae_composite"}) {
    const auto prediction =
        n::models::MaePatches(n::cast(find(name).reshape({200, 28, 28, 1}), n::DType::Float64));
    errors.push_back((n::sum(n::square(prediction - target) * n::expand_dims(hidden, 2), {1, 2}) /
                      (49. * n::sum(hidden, {1})))
                         .to_vector<double>());
  }
  int    wins  = 0;
  double limit = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < 200; ++i) {
    wins += errors[1][i] < errors[0][i];
    limit = std::max({limit, errors[0][i], errors[1][i]});
  }
  std::print("MAE lower hidden MSE on {}/200 cases; every case is plotted.\n", wins);
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.points(errors[0], errors[1], "all test cases", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .lines({0, limit}, {0, limit}, "equal error", dm::RGBA{100, 116, 139}, 1.5)
      .title("Per-case hidden errors / points below diagonal favour MAE")
      .x_label("fitting-only mean hidden MSE")
      .y_label("MAE composite hidden MSE")
      .x_limits(0, limit * 1.25)
      .y_limits(0, limit * 1.05)
      .save_svg("build/restoration_case_errors.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
MAE lower hidden MSE on 15/200 cases; every case is plotted.
\image(figures/restoration_case_errors.svg)
// result_end

\caption(All 200 cases appear. The diagonal compares the two completion rules within each case; it neither changes global MSE nor selects gallery rows.)
\alttext(A scatter compares each test case's masked-model hidden MSE against its fitting-mean hidden MSE, with an equal-error diagonal.)

> Evidence and limits

The application checks all three stores for immutability, code/prediction invariance to
hidden-value replacement, and exact copying of visible pixels. The optional independent
NumPy oracle recomputes 156,800 Gaussian values, 627, 200 corrupted pixels, 1,593,600 forward values,
all 200 masks, every denoising MSE/PSNR and all four hidden MSEs. It checks that full masked
composite MSE is 0.75 times hidden MSE and never fits or prepares report data:

```
python3 scripts/check_autoencoder_restoration.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.3_applications/build/restoration
```

Dense inference costs O(B×784×32); the masked network processes four encoder tokens and
sixteen decoder tokens, with width-squared projections and token-squared attention. Patch
visibility/composition is O(BPD) and uses no parameters. These small finite checkpoints show
mechanisms and failure modes, not photorealism, semantic completion or a general ranking of
architectures. The four sensitivity conditions are reported together; none tunes the frozen models.
